comment author Shinryuu
comment v6.6: v6.5 with a faster Wily 5 Crash Man refight (9 frames). Mega Man fires his first Air Shooter volley on the first input frame, before Crash Man can react, and his next B press only makes Crash Man jump. Two tornadoes of that first volley make hits 1 and 2, each 10 frames earlier than in v6.5. A third volley, fired from a short hop near the left wall, kills Crash Man 10 frames earlier. His bomb now explodes after the kill, so the lag frame it caused is gone. The exit comes 9 game frames earlier; the wait before the Metal Man refight rounds that to 8, and the removed lag frame makes it 9 for the rest of the movie. Mega Man takes one 4-HP hit from touching Crash Man, which costs no time. Re-synced after the fight: the hub walks to the Metal and Flash capsules, and six Metal Blade throw directions in the Wily Machine fight (81781 R+U, 81785 R, 81787 L+U, 81951 R+D, 81953 R+D, 81978 R+D), so that the weapon slots carry the sub-pixel values the Wily 6 Item 1 platforms need. v6.5: v6.4 with the lag frame in the Wily 5 Heat Man refight removed. Right after his first bubble Mega Man stops in the air for 4 frames, so Heat Man's three opening fireballs, which aim at him, land about 5 pixels further left and one of them is gone one frame sooner; the frame that used to lag then finishes in time. The first hit lands on the same game frame, and re-timed steps (a hop one frame later and a short walk past Heat Man and back) keep his random 31-frame wait and bring Mega Man, Heat Man and the random number back to exactly v6.4's state, so everything after comes 1 frame earlier. v6.4: v6.3 with the Wily 4 Boobeam fight lagging 4 times instead of 5. During the zip through the wall before the Boobeam corridor, Mega Man throws the Leaf Shield down instead of left, so the zip is not interrupted and he is 2 frames ahead; one blank frame more in the next weapon menu gives one back, so he reaches the Boobeam door 1 frame sooner. The health fill still ends on the same frame, but the boss music, which starts at the door, is now 1 frame further along during the fight, and one of its lag frames disappears. Everything after it, the alien's death included, comes 1 frame earlier. v6.3: v6.2 with the Heat Man refight won 2 frames sooner, so the Air Man refight fills 4 frames earlier (its 4-frame fill step needed only 2) and everything after it, the alien's death included, comes 4 frames earlier. After the first hit the Heat Man fight lasts 276 frames plus one frame for every 4 pixels between him and Mega Man at the start of each dash, and he moves 4 pixels a frame toward Mega Man during the dash, so he dies wherever his last dash leaves him. Mega Man now hops in place before the third dash, which is then only 12 pixels long instead of 24, and walks left with a jump before the last one, so Heat Man dashes 64 pixels instead of 60 and dies at X 76 at 77706 instead of X 68 at 77708. A decoy bubble thrown left takes one weapon slot so that the next bubble, thrown right after a one-frame turn, sits on the slot that is checked on the frame Heat Man turns vulnerable, and Mega Man walks left into the exit on the next frame. With the frame counter 4 lower the Wily 5 refights are put back in step: the Air Man capsule is touched on another subpixel (same tornado layout), the Wood Man exit hop starts a frame later (same Bubble Man pattern), the walk to the Quick Man capsule jumps a frame later, one press in that fight is Right instead of Left and its exit is re-timed, the Air Shooter shot in the hub before Crash Man is fired 14 frames later (its tornadoes set the stale subpixels that the Crash Man fight, the Wily Machine and the Wily 6 platforms read), the path to the Metal Man capsule and one inch in that fight change, and the walk to the Flash Man capsule is re-found. In the Wily Machine one first-phase blade is thrown with up+down, so it stands still and still hits on the next frame, and one second-phase blade and the killing blade are thrown straight right instead of up-right; the one spare Item-1 platform is thrown during the first fall in Wily 6, so the platform seeds stay in range (53 9F 4F) and the Item-1 energy runs out exactly on the alien's ledge platform. v6.2: v6.1 with the second Wily Machine phase beaten 1 frame sooner, on a frame that lets the stage load after it lag 4 times instead of 5, so Wily 6 starts and the movie ends 1 frame earlier. The kill now lands on the odd weapon slot, so the second phase can no longer keep a decoy there: Mega Man throws the transition decoy straight up so it leaves before the fight, and he fights from the machine's right side (13 even-slot hits, the low phase, then a blade thrown up-right, which the machine deflects up-left, holds the even slot while ten point-blank throws on the odd slot finish the machine at 82014; that blade leaves the screen on the kill frame). The reservoir blade keeps the even slot's stale subpixel from the first phase, so the first phase now sets it: Mega Man moves right one frame later and throws an up-right blade there that hits on the next frame, the slot's second blade is thrown 1 frame later and two others fly straight or stand still, so the slot's diagonal moves add up to 25 (the 28 hits stay on the same frames) and the Wily 6 platform seeds stay in range (4D 87 4B). The Metal Blade energy covers every throw (29 + 3 + 27 = 59). v6.1: v6.0 with the first Wily Machine phase beaten 3 frames sooner, so the second phase fills and dies 4 frames earlier; the stage load after it then meets a heavier music frame and lags once more, so the movie is 3 frames shorter. Mega Man opens the first phase with a 1-frame hop and two full jumps. A blade thrown with up+down as he passes over the machine's path parks motionless just left of it on the odd weapon slot, and the machine, moving left, walks into it 24 frames later, so the hits keep a 2- or 3-frame rhythm while he is low; a blade thrown straight down then holds the even slot so that the last ten throws go to the odd slot, and it leaves the screen just after the last of them (28 hits from 81785 to the kill at 81844, Mega Man untouched). Before the rolling ball hits him he parks a stationary blade for the first hit of the second phase, then throws the decoy on the floor as he jumps and the reservoir blade near the top of the jump. The second phase keeps its 62-frame fight with re-timed jumps and blade directions, eight blades thrown point-blank hit on the frame they are thrown, the Metal Blade energy covers every throw (29 + 3 + 27 = 59) and the Wily 6 platform seeds stay in range. v6.0: v5.9 with the first Wily Machine phase beaten 2 frames sooner, so the second phase fills and dies 4 frames earlier. Mega Man jumps 3 frames earlier and throws his second floor blade straight down, so it only holds the odd weapon slot while his third blade, thrown in the air, takes an even slot and hits 3 frames sooner; he then steers left and right in the air so the remaining hits keep a 2- or 3-frame rhythm. His last throw, on the kill frame, is a stationary blade parked low on the odd slot: it is the decoy of the second phase, so the transition only places the first-hit blade and the reservoir blade (v5.9 also needed a filler and a decoy), and the Metal Blade energy covers every throw (31 + 2 + 26 = 59). The second phase keeps its 62-frame fight with re-timed jumps and blade directions, and the Wily 6 platform seeds stay in range. v5.9: v5.8 with two Wily 4 lag frames removed for the cost of one. One more frame in the Wily 4 weapon menu (closing START one frame later) runs the frame counter one higher through room 32; Mega Man, invincible after the hit there, is then not drawn on the two frames where the homing enemies aim, so neither frame lags; one dropped Left keeps his fall. The higher counter also ends the Boobeam fill one frame sooner, and the fight gets one music-phase lag, so the net is 1 frame. v5.8: v5.7 with one lag frame removed in the Heat Man refight. On the frame Heat Man's second fireball lands and spawns a fire pillar, Mega Man has turned left and gives no input, so that frame finishes in time; he holds A one frame longer in the jump before it, so his landing sound starts on the same music frame as in v5.7. He ends up 4 pixels behind, which changes no hit, and two re-timed steps on the walk to the exit keep the exit; the kill, the exit and everything after come 1 frame earlier. v5.7: v5.6 with the Quick Man refight fill 4 frames earlier. The Wily 2 boss is now beaten with 39 Metal Blades instead of 42 (two blocks are killed by parked stationary blades; the Wily 2 end is on the same frame), which saves the Metal Blade unit a faster Bubble Man refight needs: Bubble Man dies 5 frames sooner with 8 blades, every hit at the 19-frame minimum (two stationary blades in his path, and one extra blade holding slot 4 so the last three hits land on slot 3). The Quick Man refight keeps its pattern with three re-timed steps (Mega Man's subpixel for the boss's random jumps); one extra Air Shooter shot on the hub walk to the Crash capsule restores the tornado slot subpixels the Crash Man refight needs; the Metal capsule is entered with a re-picked subpixel so Metal Man still makes his low jump; three Wily Machine Metal Blade throws change direction so every hit stays on its frame and the Wily 6 platform seeds stay in range. v5.6: v5.5 with one lag frame removed in Bubble Man's stage: an A press removes a lag in the second spike zip, Mega Man stays in the water one frame longer, and one extra frame in the Metal Blade menu puts the DelayDownScroll check back on a heavy music frame; the Bubble Man fill then ends 1 frame earlier with the same frame counter. v5.5: v5.4 with the Metal Man refight fill 4 frames earlier: the Crash Man refight is 1 frame faster (the second Air Shooter volley comes 1 frame earlier from a different jump, so the second hit lands on slot 4 and the kill on slot 3 one frame sooner) and the hub pause uses the up+down menu trick; the Metal capsule is entered with a re-picked subpixel so Metal Man still makes his low jump, and the Flash capsule walk is re-timed; two Wily Machine Metal Blade throws turned up-right keep every hit on the same frame with the new stale subpixels and the Wily 6 platform seeds in range. v5.4: both Wily Machine fights faster (Wily 6 starts 8 frames earlier). v5.3: alien fight 2 frames faster (pause-menu up+down cursor trick flips the hit parity; Mega Man ends his stun at X 37.06 on the secret ledge). v5.2: one lag frame removed before Wily 4 (Mega Man hops into Metal Man's boss door). v5.1: combined movie. Shinryuu's unpublished, faster run (reconstructed from his video) from the start to Wily 4, combined with our improvements (v3 Guts Tank fight, v4.1 Wily 4, v4.2 Wily 5/6) and two Wily 5 refight levers: the Air Man refight is 11 frames faster (Leaf Shield deployed right after the first hit and thrown while Mega Man rises, between the tornado rows), so the Wood Man fill ends 12 frames earlier; the Metal Man refight is 2 frames faster and the Flash capsule is reached 1 frame sooner, so the Flash Man fill ends 4 frames earlier. Refight RNG re-synced through capsule subpixels; Wily 6 platform seeds set with Metal Blade knobs. 284 frames faster than publication 4410.
